# Dependency install scripts are off.
#
# better-sqlite3 13 ships prebuilt binaries and loads them first, but npm
# drops its `gypfile: false` when it installs from package-lock.json and runs
# `node-gyp rebuild` anyway (https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/9837). Without
# a C++ toolchain (Visual Studio Build Tools, make) that makes `npm ci` and a
# fresh `npm install` fail. No other dependency needs its install script:
# esbuild finds its binary at runtime, and electron-winstaller (Squirrel) and
# fsevents (macOS) are not used by our builds.
#
# It also keeps a compromised dependency from running code on install.
#
# Side effects:
# - npm skips pre/post hooks, so scripts chain their steps with && instead.
# - `prepare` does not run on install: run `npm run prepare` once after
#   cloning to install the git hooks (husky).
# - If a new dependency needs its install script, run `npm rebuild <package>`.
ignore-scripts=true
